  "query_preview": "..\n(Tonight through next Monday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Current satellite loop is showing mid\nand high-level clouds streaming across northern and central \nNevada this morning. Further west in the eastern Pacific, the \nnext storm system can be seen spinning off the coast of \nCalifornia. There are a few weak returns on radar but nothing \nmeasurable is reported on remote observation platforms.\n\nFor today, all models are showing the upper level system over the\neast Pacific moving towards California and into western Nevada\nwith its effects seen a little later this afternoon and evening.\nFor most of today, expect peeks of sunshine with the clouds and\noccasional afternoon breezes to 15 to 20 mph. High temperatures\nthis afternoon will be in the 50s, which is just shy above normal.\nRain and snow showers are expected to develop later this afternoon\nand continue into the overnight hours tonight. Lows will be in the\n30s and 40s. Snow levels are expected to start above 6500 feet,\ngradually lowering to about 6000 to 6500 feet during the\novernight. Snow amounts at the aforementioned elevations will be\nup to a half-inch or so, with up to and inch or so along the\nhighest passes and summits. \n\nBy Wednesday, a shortwave ridge will transit the forecast area,\nbringing partly to mostly sunny skies and afternoon temperatures\nin the 40s and 50s. Models are showing a weak impulse moving\nthrough the area late Wednesday and Thursday but not too much in\nthe way of precipitation is expected with this feature. Overnight\nlows through Wednesday night will be in the 20s and 30s. Highs on\nThursday will be in the 50s. Winds are expected to remain light.\n\nFor Thursday through the weekend, models are showing a ridge of\nhigh pressure building across the southwestern United States. This\nwill bring a period of quieter weather to northern and central\nNevada. A warming trend will commence with highs gradually\nreaching the upper 50s and 60s with overnight lows in the 20s and\n30s. Winds are expected to remain light through the period.\n\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: No adjustments were needed to be\nmade to the NBM model output. Confidence is high regarding warm\nafternoon highs today. Confidence in the upcoming low pressure \nsystem is high with light, showery precipitation expected across \nportions of northern and central Nevada later this afternoon \nthrough early Wednesday morning. Moderate forecast confidence \nregarding dry weather Wednesday through at least Sunday. Moderate \nforecast confidence in gradual warming Thursday through Sunday.",
